#+TITLE: cadgui-5-3d-file — 3D file support (OpenCASCADE + ACIS round-trip)
#+STATUS: DEFERRED
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: cadgui-3-2d-parity
#+TARGET: release 3.0
#+BRANCH: qt6-gui
#+DATE: 2026-11-16
#+PARENT: cadgui-release-3.0-epic

* Context

Phase 5 of [[cadgui-release-3.0-epic]]. The separable, demand-gated 3D module --
and the LONG POLE of the whole epic. 3D is kept off the 2D critical path: a
customer can get a shippable 2D CAD (phases 1-4) without any of this.

* Background (why it is the pole)

- *OpenCASCADE (OCCT)*: an open-source B-rep solid-modelling kernel (the geometry
  engine). cadgui would represent/tessellate solids with it.
- *ACIS*: the proprietary kernel AutoCAD's solids are built on; DWG stores solids
  as an embedded ACIS stream (SAT text / SAB binary). "ACIS round-trip" = read a
  DWG's ACIS solid, translate it to an OCCT B-rep, edit/regenerate, and write a
  valid ACIS stream back -- the hard, validation-heavy part. Faithful round-trip
  on real-world solids, not toy boxes, is what sets the calendar.

* Deliverables

- OCCT integration: represent + tessellate solids; the OCCT build/link into the
  cadgui shell (C++).
- ACIS SAT/SAB read + write; the ACIS <-> OCCT B-rep translation.
- 3D DWG round-trip (solids, surfaces, meshes).
- 3D display: tessellated rendering, basic visual styles (wireframe/shaded).

* Pre-work (carried from the epic, was deferred)

- *Verify current-version 3D UX specifics against vendor docs* (was a deferred
  TODO): before scoping the 3D UX, confirm against up-to-date AutoCAD/BricsCAD
  docs how each does 3D modelling UI (direct modelling vs history, visual styles,
  gizmos), citing doc pages + versions. Feeds [[cadgui-6-3d-gui]]. Needs web/doc
  access; do it when this phase opens.

* Dependencies / sequencing

After [[cadgui-3-2d-parity]] (2D complete). Demand-gated: start only on customer
need. OCCT robustness + ACIS round-trip validation on real models dominate the
variance, not code volume.

* Test & doc approach

- A corpus of real 3D DWGs: read ACIS -> OCCT -> write ACIS, assert geometric
  equality within tolerance.
- OCCT operations unit-tested (tessellation, boolean ops) headless.
- Doc: a 3D-file section of the cadgui spec + the ACIS/OCCT translation notes.

* Acceptance themes

- [ ] Read a DWG's ACIS solids, tessellate + display them (offscreen).
- [ ] ACIS SAT and SAB read + write.
- [ ] A corpus of real 3D DWGs round-trips (ACIS<->OCCT) within tolerance.
- [ ] Basic visual styles (wireframe/shaded) render offscreen.
